            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Christopher Meis",
                        "email": "christopher.meis@gmx.de",
                        "username": "ChriMarMe"
                    },
                    "message": "Adds a more fine grained error messaging. LGTM"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2201,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This doesn't look correct.  Privileges are managed by bmcweb, so if dbus is rejecting the request, likely we need something like \"cannot be deleted\""
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2201,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "The \"Insufficient Privilege\" message was used because it is expected by the Robot test and I couldn't find a more suitable response type that is compliant with the Redfish spec."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2201,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "marking as done as it is somewhat expected by the robot test and other implementations."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2201,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": ">it is expected by the Robot test\n\nSorry, robot test isn't a spec source for what the \"correct\" error code is.  Please reference the Redfish specification.\n\nin this case, I suspect something like PropertyValueExternalConflict would be more appropriate?\n\nReally we need a ResourceDeletionConflict message registry entry to pair with ResourceCreationConflict"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2201,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "> Sorry, robot test isn't a spec source for what the \"correct\" error code is.  Please\n\nFair enough. I was looking for a more suitable error code before going with what the robot test has done, but failed on that.\n\nAs @Jen_Huang@jabil.com has pointed out (to which I agree), \"ResourceCannotBeDeleted\" is more suitable for this case, which I've implemented with PS 3.\n\n> Really we need a ResourceDeletionConflict message registry entry to pair with ResourceCreationConflict\n\nTotally agreeing on that. I'd look into raising this on the Redfish forum as suggestion."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2207,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "This isn't an acceptable sized lambda.  Please break this out into an appropriate callback."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2207,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "I should've read the common errors doc ^^'\n\nFixed in PS 2. Thanks for your review!"
                }
            ],
