                    },
                    "message": "@ed@tanous.net Would you mind taking another look on this?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "There's issues here that were pointed out and ignored.  I've left some replies, but if you need clarification on anything, happy to have a discussion, no need to make a general ping for review until everything is resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2175,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "this is unreachable, bmcweb validates account URLs pre\u2011D-Bus."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2175,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "?? This is literally the validation during the the call and it returns `UnknownObject`:\n\n```\nBreakpoint 1, redfish::processAfterDeleteUser (asyncResp=..., username=..., ec=..., m=...)\n    at /usr/src/debug/bmcweb/1.0+git/redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp:2175\n2175            if (em == \"org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.UnknownObject\")\n\n(gdb) print e->name\n$2 = 0x10b5a10 \"org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.UnknownObject\"\n```"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2175,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "@vijaysankarr@ami.com it sounds like this is up for debate that is easily solved.  Can you please run the tests listed in the commit message, and see if you can hit this code?  There's no need to argue about this when it's easily verifiable even in a qemu build."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2175,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Vijaysankar Ravi",
                        "email": "vijaysankarr@ami.com",
                        "username": "Vijaysankarr"
                    },
                    "message": "This error handling is valid, hits org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.UnknownObject for non-existent user."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2180,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "jenhuang-jabil",
                        "email": "Jen_Huang@jabil.com",
                        "username": "jenhuang-jabil"
                    },
                    "message": "Technically speaking, D-Bus NotAllowed is not semantically equivalent to Redfish InsufficientPrivilege.\n\nThe bmcweb gateway strictly validates AssignedPrivileges against the Redfish PrivilegeRegistry. \n\nIn contrast, NotAllowed indicates a backend policy restriction.\nThe exact match in the MessageRegistry is ResourceCannotBeDeleted as alternative.\n\nReference - https://redfish.dmtf.org/registries/Base.1.23.0.json"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2180,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "I believe this is the same thing I mentioned on patchset 1.  Still needs resolved."
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/account_service.hpp",
                    "line": 2180,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Tan Siewert",
                        "email": "tan@siewert.io",
                        "username": "sinuscosinustan"
                    },
                    "message": "Acknowledged.\n\nIf further discussion is wanted on this then I'd like to keep it in the PS 1 thread by Ed."
                }
